@* DS parity — no consumer yet. The card, the grid and the divider are the Razor
   equivalents the design system's record-card rules require "before any page migrates";
   the pilot list (record-card-rules.html: Accounts hardest, Subscriptions fastest) is the
   change that gives this its first consumer. *@

@*
    OdsInfoTileGrid — the auto-fitting grid the record card's Details slot is made of
    (Odyssey Design System · components/InfoTileGrid).

    Codifies the rule rather than leaving each page to re-declare a grid: tiles fit at
    minmax(200px, 1fr), so a full-width card body gets three or four per row instead of
    two, and an OdsInfoTile with Wide spans the row for prose.

    The grid holds the record's FULL field set, including fields the collapsed header
    already shows — at tile scale each value arrives with its own label, so a repeat
    reads as a field rather than an echo. There is no tile ceiling.

    A field with no value renders NO tile. The exception is a field whose absence is
    itself the fact (a subscription with no end date is open-ended) — decided per field,
    with the reason in a comment, never as the default. Tiles never condition on each
    other: each renders on its own field, never because a sibling "already shows that".
    A derived tile (Status, coverage, review state) summarises the record and carries the
    date its state began; the fields it is computed from keep their own tiles, so a fact
    cannot vanish when one state takes precedence over another.

    Dense drops the icon chips and fits at minmax(152px) — an option for record types
    whose facts are many and short (tax statements). Decided per record type, never mixed
    inside one card.

    Inside an OdsRecordCard the grid reads --rec / --rec-soft from the card and maps them
    onto the InfoTile accent, so every tile's icon chip carries the record's type colour
    with nothing passed per tile. A tile may still override with IconColor / IconSoft, but
    inside a record card it should not need to.
*@

<div class="@GridClass" style="@Style">@ChildContent</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>Seven or more facts: drop the icon chips and fit tiles at minmax(152px).
    /// Per record type, never mixed inside one card.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Dense { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Extra CSS class(es) appended to the root.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Class { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public string? Style { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The tiles. Six is the target, eight the ceiling; one may be Wide.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    private string GridClass =>
        string.Join(' ', new[] { "odc-tilegrid", Dense ? "dense" : null, Class }
            .Where(c => !string.IsNullOrEmpty(c)));
}
